            "title": "Relative Open Graph images no longer resolve against the current page URL",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/plugins/helper/open_graph.js",
            "line": 91,
            "explanation": "The new code always prefixes relative image paths with '/' and concatenates them to config.url. For a page at a nested URL (for example, config.url = 'https://example.com/blog' and the page URL is 'https://example.com/blog/foo/bar/index.html'), an image path 'test.jpg' now becomes 'https://example.com/blog/test.jpg' instead of the page-relative 'https://example.com/blog/foo/bar/test.jpg'.",
            "suggestion": "Resolve non-absolute image paths against the current page URL when available (or at least against the page directory), falling back to config.url only when no page URL is present.",
